nodecode-memory-select is a rewrite of Pinutss's Pinutss/jev-memory-selector:

  https://github.com/Pinutss/jev-memory-selector
  commit 87bd9be2a67d380024be194e6d80a1a053024361

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Pinuts (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's deterministic selector (selector.py,
tokens.py, models.py and security/redaction.py) as Common Lisp behind one
Nodecode tool, memory_select, with the same name, the same arguments and the
same answer shape as the plugin's MCP tool, plus the section, the manual topic
and the eval verb the cell contract gives it.

What was left out: the optional remote judges (the JEV decision API and an
OpenAI-compatible gateway's chat model), the single-page demo and the HTTP
server and CLI that served them, and the MCP stdio server itself, which
Nodecode's tool seam replaces. The default path the plugin ran when no JEV key
was set - the local heuristic - is the one this cell implements: nothing is
fetched at run time and no request leaves the image.
